    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Assume that $0\\leq g_{t,i}\\leq G$, for all $t=1, \\dots, T$, $i=1, \\dots, d$, where $d\\geq 1$. Then, Algorithm~\\ref{alg:tsallis} satisfies \\[ \\E[\\Regret_T] \\leq 32 G \\sqrt{(d-1) T}~. \\]"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Paper's d is the number of arms K. Re-derivation of Zimmert & Seldin's bound (authors claim no novelty for the proof; constants worse, d-1 instead of d). Paper states the adversarial losses are deterministic, so oblivious adversary; expectation over algorithm randomness. Learning rate does not depend on T, hence anytime."
  },
